{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DCPvK4dfzYeyGS9F7EfJRp","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: ship\n3\tdescription: \"Use when shipping work end-to-end. Names branch, commits, pushes, creates PR — no confirmation. Triggers: ship, ship it, send it, go from uncommitted changes to open PR.\"\n4\tmetadata:\n5\t  dependencies:\n6\t    - branch-name\n7\t    - commit\n8\t    - commits-squash\n9\t    - push\n10\t    - pr-create\n11\t---\n12\t\n13\t# Ship\n14\t\n15\tRun the full workflow: name the branch, commit, push, and open a PR. Each step runs unconditionally — the step itself decides whether to act or skip. Stop immediately if any step fails.\n16\t\n17\tIf the user says \"ship draft\" or \"draft\", create the PR as a draft.\n18\t\n19\t## Pre-run state\n20\t\n21\tThese commands run automatically when the skill loads — output replaces each line below:\n22\t\n23\t- Working tree status: !`git status`\n24\t- Current branch: !`git branch --show-current`\n25\t- Workflow count: !`gh api repos/{owner}/{repo}/actions/workflows --jq '.total_count' 2>/dev/null || true`\n26\t\n27\t## Step 1 — Name the branch\n28\t\n29\tFollow the `branch-name` skill to analyze the branch contents and rename if needed.\n30\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01AYNdbHLKcs4aZiRjRox6Fj","session_id":"69a482d3-3134-43a5-90c0-a00b8e39408a","uuid":"206f4cd3-b90f-417d-a723-1c60e005b4f7","timestamp":"2026-05-27T06:09:28.471Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Find friction in CLI/tests"}
