{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012oydevUWKqkdQt3wqhnRQs","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t#!/usr/bin/env bash\n2\t# lib/loops/ralph.sh — the ralph loop adapter.\n3\t#\n4\t# One file owns everything the engine needs to know about how to launch and\n5\t# control the ralph loop. Auto-discovered by lib/loops.sh from lib/loops/*.sh.\n6\t#\n7\t# Contract (called as almanac_loop_ralph_<verb>):\n8\t#   launch        — interactive config + exec. Used by lib/loop-launcher.sh's\n9\t#                   dispatch (no central case-statement on loop type).\n10\t#   launch_usage  — the --help text printed for this loop's launcher.\n11\t#   exec_argv     — populate _ALMANAC_LOOP_ARGV with the runner exec tokens\n12\t#                   for a given mode/prd/iterations. The ralph runner path lives\n13\t#                   HERE (not hard-coded in the launcher).\n14\t#   new_run_argv  — emit the hub's \"new run\" launcher argv (one token per line,\n15\t#                   starting with the `almanac` subcommand) from key=val pairs.\n16\t#                   The hub composes runs without knowing ralph's flag shape.\n17\t#   new_run_env   — emit KEY=VALUE env lines for fields that ride on environment\n18\t#                   (none for ralph; the verb exists so the dispatch in lib/run.sh\n19\t#                   has no `case \"$type\"` branches).\n20\t#\n21\t# Control contract (signal_file) inherits the default `.ralph-stop` / `.ralph-steer`\n22\t# convention from lib/loops.sh — no adapter override needed.\n23\t#\n24\t# The launch verb uses helpers defined in lib/loop-launcher.sh\n25\t# (_almanac_launch_need_provider/_choice/_positive_int, almanac_loop_launch_summary)\n26\t# and the shared UI / provider seams. The launcher sources those before\n27\t# dispatching, so the adapter need not source them itself.\n28\t\n29\t# Build ralph's runner exec command into _ALMANAC_LOOP_ARGV (the launcher execs\n30\t# it). MODE selects the runner: `once` runs a single iteration (once.sh PRD),\n31\t# `afk` runs autonomously (afk.sh PRD ITERATIONS). The ralph runner scripts live\n32\t# under the ralph-loop skill — this adapter is the single place that path is\n33\t# named, so the launcher no longer hard-codes …/ralph-loop/scripts/…. Returns 2\n34\t# for an unknown mode. Requires $ALMANAC_HOME (set by every entry point).\n35\talmanac_loop_ralph_exec_argv() {\n36\t  local mode=\"$1\" prd=\"$2\" iterations=\"${3:-}\"\n37\t  local scripts=\"$ALMANAC_HOME/skills/loop/ralph-loop/scripts\"\n38\t  case \"$mode\" in\n39\t    once) _ALMANAC_LOOP_ARGV=(bash \"$scripts/once.sh\" \"$prd\") ;;\n40\t    afk)  _ALMANAC_LOOP_ARGV=(bash \"$scripts/afk.sh\" \"$prd\" \"$iterations\") ;;\n41\t    *) return 2 ;;\n42\t  esac\n43\t  return 0\n44\t}\n45\t\n46\t# Interactive config + exec for the ralph loop. Parses native flags, prompts for\n47\t# any missing field via the gum-or-plain UI seam, exports the role-config env,\n48\t# and execs the runner via the exec_argv verb. Called by lib/loop-launcher.sh's\n49\t# adapter dispatch — no central code branches on loop type.\n50\talmanac_loop_ralph_launch() {"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01AYNdbHLKcs4aZiRjRox6Fj","session_id":"69a482d3-3134-43a5-90c0-a00b8e39408a","uuid":"309d7427-50f7-428d-83ee-32d94c04e839","timestamp":"2026-05-27T06:09:31.794Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Find friction in CLI/tests"}
