Low priority if design is \"lock in new code\" without retrofitting legacy.\n\n### 4. **Test coverage of private helpers vs module interface**\n**Files:** `tests/test-run.sh`, `tests/test-worker.sh`  \n**Problem:** Tests heavily exercise internal TSV-record helpers (`test_worker_health_of_reads_state`, etc., lines 803+) and private `worker_dir`/`worker_file` paths. These are implementation details, not the module's public API.  \n**Root cause:** No explicit public interface boundary — all exported functions callable and testable.  \n**Scope:** Identify the actual public API (`worker.sh` exports). Document which tests are for public contracts vs internal verification.  \n**Win-or-judgment:** Judgment call — the tests are defensive and catch refactoring hazards. May be worth keeping as \"deep regression tests\" if the module is volatile; otherwise suggests the module needs clearer contracts.\n\n### 5. **Converge.sh and Ralph.sh parameter parsing duplication**\n**Files:** `cmd/converge.sh` (146 lines), `cmd/ralph.sh` (11 lines)  \n**Problem:** converge.sh re-implements `while [ \"$#\" -gt 0 ]` flag parsing with identical error-handling patterns. ralph.sh delegates to launcher.  \n**Scope:** Converge is also a loop; could converge adapter own its flag parsing in `lib/loops/converge.sh` (already 12.3KB).  \n**Win-or-judgment:** Win — same refactor as #1. Three loops, three parsers today; should be one seam.\n\n### 6. **Install/uninstall near-perfect symmetry masks shared logic**\n**Files:** `cmd/install.sh` (213 lines), `cmd/uninstall.sh` (212 lines)  \n**Problem:** Both walk `almanac_list_skills`, manage `~/.claude/commands/almanac` and `~/.claude/skills/almanac` symlinks. Only difference is create vs remove. CLAUDE.md (line 49) mandates \"Changes to install symlink layout go in `cmd/install.sh` — don't fork the logic.\"  \n**Scope:** Extract symmetric operations (iterate skills, validate dirs, clean dangling links) into `lib/install-common.sh`; reduce code drift risk.  \n**Win-or-judgment:** Win — uninstall has already diverged (handles old dir-symlink migrations install doesn't); shared helpers prevent future skew.\n\n### 7. **Skill metadata dependency validation is a no-op**\n**File:** `lib/almanac-core.sh`  \n**Problem:** CLAUDE.md line 30 says \"Declare hard deps in `metadata.dependencies`; validation fails if a listed dep doesn't exist.\" Five skills declare dependencies (`ship`, `task-start`, `pr-watch`, `agents-md-fix`). No test verifies those targets exist or are complete.  \n**Scope:** Add to `almanac_validate_skill()`: read `metadata.dependencies` array, confirm each named skill exists and has valid SKILL.md.  \n**Win-or-judgment:** Win — low friction; catches skill removal bugs early.\n\n### 8. **Test split has drifted slightly**\n**Files:** `tests/test-structure.sh`, `tests/test-skills.sh`  \n**Problem:** test-structure.sh (lines 21–44) checks for hardcoded CLI scripts and skill files — it's layout validation. But it also sources `lib/almanac-core.sh` (line 7) for functions that never get called. test-skills.sh owns the content validation.  \n**Scope:** test-structure.sh should not source lib/almanac-core.sh. Remove the import; keep layout checks only.  \n**Win-or-judgment:** Judgment call — harmless today but violates the split rule in CLAUDE.md line 36.\n\n---\n\n**Summary:** Four clear wins (ralph/harden CLI duplication refactor, CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR fix, dependency validation, test split clarification) + two judgment calls (raw echo cleanup, test coverage philosophy) + one symmetry improvement (install/uninstall shared logic). Total scope: ~500 lines of refactoring to surface, ~3-4 foundational cleanup commits."}],"totalDurationMs":71856,"totalTokens":71351,"totalToolUseCount":33,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":305,"cache_read_input_tokens":69425,"output_tokens":1618,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_inpu