{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TrzZgzhXgpvMQuHUC5vTk2","type":"tool_result","content":"200\t\n201\t  Interactive CLI:\n202\t    almanac ralph\n203\t    # or: bash {{SKILL_SCRIPTS}}/ralph.sh\n204\t\n205\t  Single iteration (HITL):\n206\t    bash {{SKILL_SCRIPTS}}/once.sh <name>\n207\t\n208\t  Autonomous (AFK):\n209\t    bash {{SKILL_SCRIPTS}}/afk.sh <name> <iterations>\n210\t\n211\t  Example — run 10 iterations:\n212\t    bash {{SKILL_SCRIPTS}}/afk.sh auth-system 10\n213\t```\n214\t\n215\tWhere `{{SKILL_SCRIPTS}}` is the absolute path to this skill's scripts. Resolve in this order:\n216\t\n217\t1. `~/.agents/skills/almanac/ralph-loop/scripts` — set by `almanac install codex`; use this when running in Codex.\n218\t2. `~/.claude/skills/almanac/ralph-loop/scripts` — set by `almanac install claude-code`; use this when running in Claude Code.\n219\t3. `${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}/scripts` — fallback if the host agent populates `CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR` from the resolved skill directory.\n220\t4. `$ALMANAC_HOME/skills/loop/ralph-loop/scripts` — fallback when invoked outside an installed provider.\n221\t\n222\tPrint the literal provider install path in user-facing instructions (`~/.agents/...` for Codex, `~/.claude/...` for Claude Code) so users can run the scripts directly.\n223\t\n224\t## Modes\n225\t\n226\t### AFK Mode (`afk.sh`)\n227\t\n228\tFully autonomous. Runs N iterations, each in a fresh agent context. Stops when:\n229\t- All tasks complete (`<promise>COMPLETE</promise>`)\n230\t- A task is blocked (`<promise>ABORT</promise>`)\n231\t- Iteration limit reached\n232\t- `.ralph-stop` file exists in the working directory (graceful stop — see below)\n233\t- Overseer detects HIGH drift (writes `.ralph-stop` automatically — see Overseer below)\n234\t\n235\t**Provider selection:** set `RALPH_PROVIDER=codex` or `RALPH_PROVIDER=claude` to force an agent. If unset, the scripts use Codex when running inside Codex, otherwise Claude Code when available, otherwise Codex.\n236\t\n237\t**Model override:** set `RALPH_MODEL` (e.g. `RALPH_PROVIDER=codex RALPH_MODEL=gpt-5.5 bash afk.sh <name> 10` or `RALPH_MODEL=claude-opus-4-7 bash afk.sh <name> 10`); unset uses the selected provider's default.\n238\t\n239\t**Thinking override:** set `RALPH_EFFORT` to control model thinking level. Codex receives this as `model_reasoning_effort`; Claude Code receives it as `--effort`. Supported common values: `low`, `medium`, `high`, `xhigh`; Claude Code also supports `max`."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69a482d3-3134-43a5-90c0-a00b8e39408a","uuid":"d42d2ca7-7f15-4d0d-a861-ccc9b2c74831","timestamp":"2026-05-27T06:10:17.374Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/jakubneumann/Documents/code/neumie/almanac/skills/loop/ralph-loop/SKILL.md","content":"\n  Interactive CLI:\n    almanac ralph\n    # or: bash {{SKILL_SCRIPTS}}/ralph.sh\n\n  Single iteration (HITL):\n    bash {{SKILL_SCRIPTS}}/once.sh <name>\n\n  Autonomous (AFK):\n    bash {{SKILL_SCRIPTS}}/afk.sh <name> <iterations>\n\n  Example — run 10 iterations:\n    bash {{SKILL_SCRIPTS}}/afk.sh auth-system 10\n```\n\nWhere `{{SKILL_SCRIPTS}}` is the absolute path to this skill's scripts. Resolve in this order:\n\n1. `~/.agents/skills/almanac/ralph-loop/scripts` — set by `almanac install codex`; use this when running in Codex.\n2. `~/.claude/skills/almanac/ralph-loop/scripts` — set by `almanac install claude-code`; use this when running in Claude Code.\n3. `${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}/scripts` — fallback if the host agent populates `CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR` from the resolved skill directory.\n4. `$ALMANAC_HOME/skills/loop/ralph-loop/scripts` — fallback when invoked outside an installed provider.\n\nPrint the literal provider install path in user-facing instructions (`~/.agents/...` for Codex, `~/.claude/...` for Claude Code) so users can run the scripts directly.\n\n## Modes\n\n### AFK Mode (`afk.sh`)\n\nFully autonomous. Runs N iterations, each in a fresh agent context. Stops when:\n- All tasks complete (`<promise>COMPLETE</promise>`)\n- A task is blocked (`<promise>ABORT</promise>`)\n- Iteration limit reached\n- `.ralph-stop` file exists in the working directory (graceful stop — see below)\n- Overseer detects HIGH drift (writes `.ralph-stop` automatically — see Overseer below)\n\n**Provider selection:** set `RALPH_PROVIDER=codex` or `RALPH_PROVIDER=claude` to force an agent. If unset, the scripts use Codex when running inside Codex, otherwise Claude Code when available, otherwise Codex.\n\n**Model override:** set `RALPH_MODEL` (e.g. `RALPH_PROVIDER=codex RALPH_MODEL=gpt-5.5 bash afk.sh <name> 10` or `RALPH_MODEL=claude-opus-4-7 bash afk.sh <name> 10`); unset uses the selected provider's default.\n\n**Thinking override:** set `RALPH_EFFORT` to control model thinking level. Codex receives this as `model_reasoning_effort`; Claude Code receives it as `--effort`. Supported common values: `low`, `medium`, `high`, `xhigh`; Claude Code also supports `max`.","numLines":40,"startLine":200,"totalLines":300}}}
