write `.converge-steer` (overwrites any prior) → slice 03's worker prompt consumes and removes\ndocs/plans/converge-loop/issues/04-overseer-verdict-steer-stop.md:43:  - [x] `CONVERGED` → `.converge-stop` written → loop exits next-iteration check → registry `status=done`\ndocs/plans/converge-loop/issues/04-overseer-verdict-steer-stop.md:44:  - [x] `STEER:<text>` → `.converge-steer` file content matches\ndocs/plans/converge-loop/issues/04-overseer-verdict-steer-stop.md:52:- The overseer is **read-only**. It never commits, never writes outside `overseer.log`, `.converge-stop`, `.converge-steer`, and `convergence.md`. Slice 05 will add `goal.md` and `goal.history.log` to its write list.\ndocs/plans/converge-loop/issues/04-overseer-verdict-steer-stop.md:55:- `--no-oversee` is the **trust knob**. Some users will want the convergence loop without the LLM judge — they'll set rounds=5, eyeball the result. Make sure this path has zero overseer-related work (no prompt, no agent call, no parsing, no `.converge-stop` writes from the overseer).\nskills/loop/ralph-loop/SKILL.md:232:- `.ralph-stop` file exists in the working directory (graceful stop — see below)\nskills/loop/ralph-loop/SKILL.md:233:- Overseer detects HIGH drift (writes `.ralph-stop` automatically — see Overseer below)\nskills/loop/ralph-loop/SKILL.md:251:2. **Wait for CI** (shell, only if step 1 actually pushed). Polls `gh run list` every `RALPH_CI_POLL_INTERVAL` seconds (default 30) for the run matching the pushed `headSha`, blocking until status leaves `in_progress|queued|waiting|requested|pending`. Times out after `RALPH_CI_WAIT_TIMEOUT` seconds (default 1800 = 30 min). Exits early on `.ralph-stop`. While the overseer waits, main-loop iterations keep running — only the overseer thread is blocked.\nskills/loop/ralph-loop/SKILL.md:261:   Outputs `DRIFT_LEVEL: low|medium|high`, `REASON: …`, `STEER: …`. On HIGH drift writes `.ralph-stop`. When `STEER` is non-`none`, writes the directive to `.ralph-steer`.\nskills/loop/ralph-loop/SKILL.md:270:- **Overseer steer** — when `.ralph-steer` exists. The spawned agent is told the overseer reviewed recent reports + commits and emitted concrete advice (wrong assumption, scope correction, alternate approach, etc.). One-shot: `afk.sh` removes the file after consumption. The overseer can re-emit it next tick if the underlying issue persists.\nskills/loop/ralph-loop/SKILL.md:297:- Graceful stop mid-run → `touch .ralph-stop` in the working directory. The loop exits at the start of the next iteration, pushes commits, removes the file. Use this instead of Ctrl+C — Ctrl+C skips the auto-push and may leave RALPH commits stranded locally.\ndocs/plans/converge-loop/issues/06-hub-integration-and-watch-controls.md:11:Wire converge runs into the shared `almanac hub` so they appear alongside ralph and harden runs in the registry view. Add `almanac converge <slug> --watch` (live dashboard, redraw loop) and `almanac converge <slug> --stop` (graceful halt via `.converge-stop`). Slice 04 already writes `.converge-stop` from the overseer; this slice exposes the same signal to the human operator.\ndocs/plans/converge-loop/issues/06-hub-integration-and-watch-controls.md:19:  - [x] `signal_file stop` → `.converge-stop`\ndocs/plans/converge-loop/issues/06-hub-integration-and-watch-controls.md:20:  - [x] `signal_file steer` → `.converge-steer`\ndocs/plans/converge-loop/issues/06-hub-integration-and-watch-controls.md:31:- [x] `almanac converge <slug> --stop` writes `.converge-stop` to the plan dir and exits 0. The running loop picks it up at its next round-boundary check and exits cleanly (registry marks `status=aborted`).\ndocs/plans/converge-loop/issues/06-hub-integration-and-watch-controls.md:36:  - [x] `almanac converge <slug> --stop` writes `.converge-stop` and the loop exits cleanly on next round\nskills/loop/converge-loop/SKILL.md:96:- optional one-shot steer directive from `.converge-steer`\nskills/loop/converge-loop/SKILL.md:158:| `CONVERGED` | Writes `.converge-stop`, exits done, writes `convergence.md`. |\nskills/loop/converge-loop/SKILL.md:159:| `STOP` | Writes `.converge-stop`, exits aborted, writes `convergence.md`. |\nskills/loop/converge-loop/SKILL.md:160:| `STEER` | Writes `.converge-steer` when `STEER` is not `none`; next worker consumes it once. |\ndocs/plans/converge-loop/prd.md:43:- `CONVERGED` / `STOP` → writes `.converge-stop`, loop exits, `convergence.md` written\ndocs/plans/converge-loop/prd.md:44:- `STEER:<directive>` → writes `.converge-steer` (one-shot for next iteration)\ndocs/plans/converge-loop/prd.md:60:8. As a developer, I want the overseer to emit one-shot steering directives (`.converge-steer`) when it has concrete advice, so that mid-run drift gets corrected without my intervention.\ndocs/plans/converge/the-almanac-codebase-improve-gives-no-major-improvements/converge-claude-iteration-1.log:19:[Omitted long matching line]\ndocs/plans/converge/the-almanac-codebase-improve-gives-no-major-improvements/converge-claude-iteration-1.log:33:[Omitted long matching line]\ndocs/plans/converge/the-almanac-codebase-improve-gives-no-major-improvements/converge-claude-iteration-1.log:39:[Omitted long matching line]\ndocs/plans/converge/the-almanac-codebase-improve-gives-no-major-improvements/converge-claude-iteration-1.log:72:[Omitted long matching line]\ndocs/plans/converge/the-almanac-codebase-improve-gives-no-major-improvements/converge-claude-iteration-1.log:114:[Omitted long matching line]\nskills/loop/ralph-loop/scripts/afk.sh:159:# .ralph-stop. No-ops gracefully if `gh` missing, no remote, no run yet\nskills/loop/ralph-loop/scripts/afk.sh:179:    [ -f .ralph-stop ] && return 0\nskills/loop/ralph-loop/scripts/afk.sh:272:# check_ci_status when CI is green) and .ralph-steer (one-shot — consumed\nskills/loop/ralph-loop/scripts/afk.sh:298:  if [ -f .ralph-steer ]; then\nskills/loop/ralph-loop/scripts/afk.sh:303:    cat .ralph-steer\nskills/loop/ralph-loop/scripts/afk.sh:307:    rm -f .ralph-steer\nski