ename), so harden-core and converge-core no longer reimplement their own `_control_file` wrapper each. The **launcher** (`lib/loop-launcher.sh`) consumes launch — `almanac_loop_launch` resolves `almanac_loop_<type>_launch` via the adapter seam and calls it; the adapter's launch verb in turn execs the runner via `almanac_loop_adapter_call <type> exec_argv …` rather than a hard-coded path — and the **hub** consumes control through `almanac_loop_run_signal_file` (above). Self-contained like `lib/agent.sh` (no dependency on `lib/core.sh` — only printf/tr/basename/source), it is its own test surface (`tests/test-loops.sh`: discovery, dispatch rejecting an unimplemented verb, the `signal_file` control mapping, and the `exec_argv` launch composition for loops against a fake `$ALMANAC_HOME`). Adding a loop is one new file under `lib/loops/`; nothing central changes."," "," ## Validation (`lib/almanac-core.sh`)"," "]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
