{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01C8xwRRDe11ieytW9YWpZcm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Couldn't execute tests — bash sandboxed and you declined the test-perms prompt — but kept changes scoped to careful pure additions plus one targeted hub refactor.\n\n## Applied improvements\n\n1. **Hub deepening (the real win)** — `cmd/hub.sh` `almanac_hub_resume_or_clone` dropped from 67 lines of per-loop `case \"$run_type\"` + the `\"$run_type\" != \"harden\" && != \"converge\"` enum into 30 lines of adapter dispatch. Added two adapter verbs:\n   - `status_to_opts <status_file>` (ralph/harden/converge) — inverts the adapter's own status schema into key=val pairs that `new_run_argv`/`new_run_env` consume\n   - `launch_backed` — defined only by ralph; signals hub `--resume` may append `--yes`. Direct-runner loops (harden, converge) leave it undefined and never get the suffix.\n   The hub now branches on loop type zero times. Adding a 4th loop = one new file in `lib/loops/`. Added 5 tests in `tests/test-run.sh` (per-loop round-trip + `launch_backed` contract). Existing `test_hub_resume_harden_does_not_append_yes` should still pass — same observable behavior.\n\n2. **`skills/loop/ralph-loop/SKILL.md`** — dropped broken `${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}/scripts` fallback (CLAUDE.md flagged this as a violation: single-file symlink can't resolve subdirs).\n\n3. **`cmd/sync.sh`** — per-skill status rows now use `_success`/`_warn`/`_error`/`_info` matching `cmd/doctor.sh`'s convention. UX shifts from `✓ name: up to date` to `[ok] name: up to date`.\n\n4. **Docs sync** — `CONTEXT.md` and `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` describe the new resume contract.\n\n## Dropped from candidates (not worth doing)\n\n- **Signal-file decoupling** — already done; only one user-facing log string left, not operational coupling.\n- **`test-structure.sh` source cleanup** — reverted; it legitimately needs `almanac_list_skills` (sanctioned walker per CLAUDE.md).\n- **`metadata.dependencies` validation** — already implemented in `almanac_validate_skill` lines 137-157 with negative test coverage.\n- **`cmd/list.sh` echo→helpers** — `echo` is the right call for data rows; rule is about error/status messages.\n\n## Verification needed from you\n\nRun: `bash tests/test-loops.sh tests/test-run.sh tests/test-hub.sh tests/test-skills.sh tests/test-converge.sh tests/test-harden-cli.sh`\n\nThe hub refactor is the only behavioral change; tests 1-3 cover it. Others are sanity (changes don't touch their modules)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":111,"cache_read_input_tokens":184281,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":111},"output_tokens":46,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"69a482d3-3134-43a5-90c0-a00b8e39408a","uuid":"657cb2d0-9828-4fbd-b1bc-b47e27169ec4","request_id":"req_011CbSbCj1CjS1Yko5jFt7Zs"}
